    "title": "<p>Differential morphological criteria in bone marrow biopsy samples for childhood myelodysplastic neoplasm with low blasts, hypocellular, and severe aplastic anaemia</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "John Kim Choi",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"width: 708.7pt; border-collapse: collapse;\" border=\"0\" width=\"945\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 103.5pt; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid black; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"138\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Lineage</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 302.6pt; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid black; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"403\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Childhood myelodysplastic neoplasm with low blasts, hypocellular</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 302.6pt; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid black; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"403\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Severe aplastic anaemia</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 103.5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"138\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Erythropoiesis</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 302.6pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"403\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Patchy distribution</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Left shift with clusters of &gt;&nbsp;20&nbsp;precursors</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Increased mitotic figures</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 302.6pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"403\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Marked decrease with foci of &lt;&nbsp;10&nbsp;cells with maturation</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 103.5pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"138\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Granulopoiesis</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 302.6pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"403\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Marked decrease with left shift</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 302.6pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"403\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Marked decrease or absence with maturation</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 103.5pt; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-bottom: 1pt solid black; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"138\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Megakaryopoiesis</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 302.6pt; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-bottom: 1pt solid black; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"403\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Marked decrease or absence</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">With or without dysplasia, including micromegakaryocytes</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 302.6pt; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-bottom: 1pt solid black; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"403\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Decrease or absence</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">No dysplasia</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>",
